 4. 🛰️ 1 science thing: &quot;Flyby&quot; satellite pics 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Images: HEO Space imagery startup HEO has raised $25 million to expand into geostationary orbit, Alex Fitzpatrick reports. 

 📸 The company uses cameras and sensors attached to satellites to take "flyby" images of other satellites and spacecraft.

 That lets space companies and governments better understand what's going on with their spacecraft and satellites — or those of adversarial nations. HEO co-founder and CEO William Crowe tells Axios: "For commercial players, it allows you to really understand what's wrong with your spacecraft. So a bunch of companies have come to us when something's wrong with their spacecraft."

